     "content": [
      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order because the dose looks unsafe.\n\nMetformin 1700 mg three times daily is 5,100 mg/day. That is twice the usual maximum of 2,550 mg/day for immediate-release metformin in adults, and it could raise the risk of lactic acidosis and GI toxicity.\n\nDid you mean one of these?\n- **850 mg PO three times daily with meals** (2,550 mg/day, the usual maximum)\n- **1,700 mg/day in total**, for example 850 mg PO twice daily with meals\n- **Another dose**, such as a lower starting dose (500 mg PO twice daily with meals)\n\nIf 1700 mg three times daily is intentional, please confirm that and I'll enter it with a note documenting the confirmation. Otherwise, tell me the corrected dose and I'll enter it right away."
      }
     ],
